ont-size:11px; color:var(--ink-3); line-height:1.5; margin-top:8px;">Automated module test</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></div><div style="background:#EAF2FB; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:40px 0;"><div style="max-width:976px; padding:0 48px;"><div class="auto-sechead"><h2>Where it&#39;s made</h2><p>Power module and power discrete assembly is run in Ayutthaya, Thailand and Jiaxing, China.</p></div><div class="auto-plants" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr);"><a class="auto-plantcard" href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;"><div><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Thailand</span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div></div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="auto-plantcard" href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;"><div><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> China</span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div></div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" style="color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; font-weight:600;">View all locations &rarr;</a></p></div></div><div style="background:var(--bg); border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:40px 0 48px;"><div style="max-width:976px; padding:0 48px;"><div class="auto-sechead"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="auto-faq"><div class="item is-open"><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">01</span><h3 class="qt">Which module formats do you build for traction inverters?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>Custom SiC modules on DBC substrate, and the HP1 and HPD formats.</p></div></div><div class="item "><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">02</span><h3 class="qt">Are the power modules AEC-Q101 qualified?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>AEC-Q101 is a qualification for discrete devices. Hana&rsquo;s TO-247 family, D2PAK-7L and TSPAK discretes are AEC-Q101 qualified. Module reliability testing, including power and thermal cycling, follows the program&rsquo;s qualification plan.</p></div></div><div class="item "><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">03</span><h3 class="qt">When is silver-sinter die attach used?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>Where the program specifies it, typically for SiC devices. Silver sinter can give better thermal and mechanical performance than solder at the higher junction temperatures and repeated thermal cycling that SiC devices see.</p></div></div></div><div style="margin-top:22px;"><a href="/markets/automotive" style="font-size:12px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.07em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; white-space:nowrap; line-height:1.4;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Automotive market hub</a></div></div></div><section class="auto-cta auto-cta--spoke" style="background:var(--hana-blue-deep);" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-accent="cyan" data-fade="none"><div class="inner"><div><h2>Have a power-module program in mind?</h2><p>Send the device specification and target volumes, and we will come back with a DFM review and an assembly plan.</p></div><div class="actions"><a href="/contact" class="auto-btn auto-btn--ondark-primary">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></div></div></section></main></div></div>

